From: Lukas Fittl <lukas@fittl.com>
Subject: [PATCH] exprLocation: Check stack depth

exprLocation recurses into the left operand of an A_Expr (and other
child nodes), without checking stack depth. The grammar calls it when
reporting errors like "multiple ORDER BY clauses not allowed", so a
deeply nested expression (e.g. "(SELECT ORDER BY a) ORDER BY x+x+...")
could overflow the stack during raw parsing, before any other check
runs.
---
 src/backend/nodes/nodeFuncs.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/backend/nodes/nodeFuncs.c b/src/backend/nodes/nodeFuncs.c
--- a/src/backend/nodes/nodeFuncs.c
+++ b/src/backend/nodes/nodeFuncs.c
@@ -1387,6 +1387,10 @@ exprLocation(const Node *expr)

 	if (expr == NULL)
 		return -1;
+
+	/* Guard against stack overflow due to overly complex expressions */
+	check_stack_depth();
+
 	switch (nodeTag(expr))
 	{
 		case T_RangeVar:
